### Note: This file is used to test and validate the Author Management Endpoints.
### It aligns perfectly with the AuthorsController routing specifications and MediatR structure.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5165/api
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Create a New Author
### Adds a new writer profile into the catalog system database records.
POST {{baseUrl}}/Authors
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "firstName": "Martin",
  "lastName": "Fowler",
  "biography": "An author, software developer, and public speaker on software architecture.",
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2. Get All Authors
### Queries the entire author catalog collection based on specified filter criteria parameters.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Authors?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3. Get Author By ID
### Resolves details for a single target author by their principal key tracker.
GET {{baseUrl}}/Authors/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4. Update Author Profile
### Modifies existing author attributes. Ensure that the URL parameter id matches the body payload Id.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Authors/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "id": 1,
  "firstName": "Martin",
  "lastName": "Fowler",
  "biography": "An updated premium biography regarding enterprise software patterns.",
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5. Delete Author Profile (Soft Delete)
### Safely moves the target author instance to an inactive deleted tracking state.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/Authors/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Restore Soft-Deleted Author
### Reverts the soft delete mutation to re-integrate the author record into the library index.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/Authors/1/restore-author
Content-Type: {{contentType}}